File "region_stack_space.ml", line 58, characters 24-51:
58 |   | hd :: tl -> f hd :: map_local_param bound tl ~f
                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Warning 222 [tmc-breaks-tailcall-region]: This call is in tail-modulo-cons
  position in a TMC function, but it is enclosed in a local-allocation region
  that cannot be closed as part of the call, so the call will not be
  transformed into a tail call and the function does not run in constant
  stack space.
  This happens when a value allocated in the region may reach the callee,
  which is the case as soon as the function takes a parameter at mode local.

